# Q6b's criterion (TASK-26, ADR-0267 point 3, ADR-0263 point 7): a terminal
# launched in a room with limits is in the room's job; `top` shows the room
# against its limit; a program that takes the room's memory makes the panel
# send the use, and the compositor puts a pill in the window's title bar at
# 90% and draws the hover card, from the panel's readings only. Coordinates
# as tests/gui/rooms.script's (logical, 1024 x 768, scale 1).
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type mkdir project\r
screen ~> _
type room new project --mem 64M --procs 16 +w ~/project\r
screen project --colour 1 --mem 64M --procs 16 +w ~/project
screen ~> _
# The chip enters the room; System+Enter launches a terminal in it.
clickc 2f7f8f 300 719 600 7
chord meta ret
origin 105 138
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen project ~/project> _
click 400 120
# The pointer leaves the title bar (the card is outside the window, above it
# or below it, so it covers no text of the terminal).
click 400 500
type top\r
prefix ROOM
prefix project
prefix session
screen project ~/project> _
type grants echo\r
prefix limits --mem 64M --procs 16  (room project)
screen project ~/project> _
shot limits-calm
# A program that keeps what it takes until the job refuses: the room is at
# its memory limit for six seconds, and the panel tells the compositor within
# a second.
type memhog --hold 6 &\r
prefix memhog: refused after
pause 2500
shot limits-pill
# The pill is in the title bar, first of the room's pills ("mem 99%", from the
# panel's reading): its fill, which the calm title bar (d3e1e5) does not have.
region 366 115 2 8 f6f9f9
# The pointer on the title bar: the hover card, above or below the window at
# its right, where no pixel of the terminal's buffer is (ADR-0172 point 1).
pointc d3e1e5 162 108 100 4
pause 400
shot limits-card
# The first terminal's shell turns the machine off.
click 400 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
origin 73 106
type poweroff\r
exit
